        {
          "question": "e-7665",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{x} & >{4}^{x-15} \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{x}-{4}^{x-15} & >0 \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{-15})\\cdot {4}^{x} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $4^{x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx^5 - 4^{-15} > 0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5} & >{4}^{-15} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{5}} & >\\sqrt[5]{{4}^{-15}} \\\\ x & >{({4}^{-15})}^{1/5} \\\\ x & >{4}^{-3} \\\\ x & >\\frac{1}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x > \\dfrac{1}{64}.$",
